"""
    PLOTLYJS_COLORSCALES

    Plotly.js's own built-in named colorscale stop tables (`[fraction, "rgb(...)"]`
    pairs), keyed by lower-case name, extracted directly from the bundled
    `plotly.min.js` (its own colour-scale registry). A classification diagram's marker
    `colorscale` is often one of these bare names (e.g. the PTX tab's own
    `classification-diagram-colormap` dropdown), resolved client-side by Plotly.js
    itself - not through Julia's `colors[Symbol(name)]` (ColorSchemes.jl), a separate,
    differently-authored implementation of similarly-named schemes with its own, not
    necessarily identical, stop colours. `svg_colorscale` checks this table first so an
    exported classification diagram's colours match what the browser actually drew,
    rather than a same-named but visually different lookalike.
